sequenceDiagram
    participant Parent as Parent Process
    participant Kernel
    participant Child as Child Process
    
    Parent->>Kernel: fork()
    Kernel->>Kernel: Duplicate process
    Kernel->>Kernel: Copy page tables (COW)
    Kernel->>Child: Create new process
    Kernel-->>Parent: Return child PID
    Kernel-->>Child: Return 0
    
    Note over Parent,Child: Both processes now running
    
    Parent->>Parent: if (pid > 0) // parent code
    Child->>Child: if (pid == 0) // child code
    
    Child->>Kernel: exec("/bin/ls", args)
    Kernel->>Kernel: Replace process image
    Kernel->>Child: Load new program
    Child->>Child: Execute /bin/ls
    
    Child->>Kernel: exit(0)
    Kernel->>Kernel: Process termination
    Kernel->>Kernel: Become zombie
    
    Parent->>Kernel: wait(&status)
    Kernel->>Kernel: Reap zombie child
    Kernel-->>Parent: Return child status
    
    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Parent,Child: Typical Unix process creation pattern
    end
